{
    "background_story": "Marshall was a brilliant and eccentric art historian with a passion for the Baroque period. His obsession with the works of Gian Lorenzo Bernini led him to spend years studying the master sculptor's techniques and inspirations. Marshall's friends and colleagues would often joke that he had a 'Bernini-esque' eye for detail, able to spot even the subtlest nuances in the artist's creations. One day, while researching in Rome, Marshall stumbled upon an obscure manuscript that hinted at the existence of a lost Bernini sculpture. Undeterred by skepticism, he embarked on a quest to uncover the truth, scouring the city's hidden archives and secret gardens. His tireless pursuit ultimately led to the discovery of a previously unknown Bernini masterpiece, earning Marshall international acclaim and cementing his reputation as a leading authority on the artist.",
